# 低频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List06核心词汇

{{chancellor}}{/ˈtʃɑːnsələr/}{总理；校长}{The chancellor announced new policies for the university.}}
{{chaos}}{/ˈkeɪɒs/}{混乱；混沌}{The sudden resignation caused chaos in the office.}}
{{characteristic}}{/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk/}{特征；特性}{Patience is a characteristic of a good teacher.}}
{{charter}}{/ˈtʃɑːtər/}{宪章；包租}{The organization operates under a strict charter.}}
{{chase}}{/tʃeɪs/}{追逐；追赶}{The dog loves to chase squirrels in the park.}}
{{cherish}}{/ˈtʃerɪʃ/}{珍爱；怀念}{She cherishes the memories of her childhood.}}
{{chip}}{/tʃɪp/}{芯片；碎片}{The company manufactures computer chips.}}
{{chorus}}{/ˈkɔːrəs/}{合唱；合唱队}{The audience joined in the chorus of the song.}}
{{chunk}}{/tʃʌŋk/}{大块；大量}{A large chunk of the budget goes to marketing.}}
{{cipher}}{/ˈsaɪfər/}{密码；零}{The message was written in cipher to prevent interception.}}
{{circulate}}{/ˈsɜːkjuleɪt/}{循环；传播}{Rumors circulated quickly among the employees.}}
{{civilian}}{/sɪˈvɪliən/}{平民；民用的}{The government prioritized civilian safety during the conflict.}}
{{clamp}}{/klæmp/}{夹子；钳制}{The mechanic used a clamp to hold the parts together.}}
{{clarification}}{/ˌklærɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/}{澄清；说明}{The manager requested clarification on the new policy.}}
{{clash}}{/klæʃ/}{冲突；碰撞}{The two groups clashed over the proposed changes.}}
{{classify}}{/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/}{分类；归类}{The books are classified by subject in the library.}}
{{clause}}{/klɔːz/}{条款；从句}{The contract includes an arbitration clause.}}
{{clergy}}{/ˈklɜːdʒi/}{神职人员}{The clergy led the community in prayer.}}
{{clinical}}{/ˈklɪnɪkl/}{临床的；冷静的}{Clinical trials are essential for new drug approval.}}
{{clone}}{/kləʊn/}{克隆；复制品}{Scientists successfully cloned the sheep in 1996.}}
{{cluster}}{/ˈklʌstər/}{簇；群}{A cluster of stars was visible in the night sky.}}
{{coalition}}{/ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn/}{联盟；联合}{The political parties formed a coalition government.}}
{{coarse}}{/kɔːs/}{粗糙的；粗俗的}{The fabric has a coarse texture.}}
{{cognitive}}{/ˈkɒɡnətɪv/}{认知的}{Cognitive development is rapid in early childhood.}}
{{coherent}}{/kəʊˈhɪərənt/}{连贯的；一致的}{The argument was clear and coherent.}}
{{coincidence}}{/kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns/}{巧合；巧事}{It was pure coincidence that we met at the airport.}}
{{collaborate}}{/kəˈlæbəreɪt/}{合作；协作}{The two departments collaborated on the research project.}}
{{collide}}{/kəˈlaɪd/}{碰撞；冲突}{The two cars collided at the intersection.}}
{{combat}}{/ˈkɒmbæt/}{战斗；反对}{New measures were introduced to combat fraud.}}
{{commemorate}}{/kəˈmeməreɪt/}{纪念；庆祝}{The monument commemorates those who fought for freedom.}}
